\section{UKG-SE v3.0 Autonomous Simulation Architecture}
\label{sec:ukgse_architecture}

\subsection{Overview}
The UKG-SE v3.0 framework, designed by C.~Matthew~Blackwell, is a hardware-accelerated,
autonomous simulation engine integrating tensor-field solvers, Hamiltonian phase-space
analysis, and a cryptographically verified state ledger. The system operates in
continuous-yield mode, enabling real-time refactoring of internal mathematical structures.

\subsection{Solver Core}
The solver core computes tensor fields $T^{\mu\nu}$ and evaluates the covariant
residual
\[
R = \left\lVert \nabla_{\mu} T^{\mu\nu} \right\rVert ,
\]
which serves as the stability metric for runtime mutation. When $R$ exceeds a
hardware-defined threshold $R_{\mathrm{crit}}$, the tensor field is dynamically
refactored according to
\[
T^{\mu\nu}_{\mathrm{new}} = \alpha\, T^{\mu\nu}_{\mathrm{old}},
\qquad 0 < \alpha < 1,
\]
representing a contraction of unstable tensor pathways.

\subsection{Hamiltonian Phase-Space Engine}
The Hamiltonian subsystem models trajectories in phase space $(q,p)$ using
\[
H(q,p) = \frac{p^{2}}{2} + V(q),
\]
with $V(q)$ representing an effective potential. Trajectories evolve via numerical
integration:
\[
q_{n+1} = q_{n} + \Delta t\, p_{n}, \qquad
p_{n+1} = p_{n} - \Delta t\, q_{n}.
\]
A divergence metric
\[
D = |q\,p|
\]
is used to identify unstable trajectories. When $D > D_{\mathrm{crit}}$, the
trajectory is pruned from the simulation.

\subsection{Secure State Ledger}
Each simulation cycle produces a ledger entry containing:
\begin{itemize}
    \item the tensor field $T^{\mu\nu}$,
    \item the residual $R$,
    \item phase-space coordinates $(q,p)$,
    \item mutation and pruning flags,
    \item a timestamp $\tau$,
    \item a SHA-3 cryptographic hash.
\end{itemize}

The ledger is stored in JSON Lines format, providing a tamper-evident,
append-only record of the system's evolution. Each entry $E$ is hashed via
\[
\mathrm{Hash}(E) = \mathrm{SHA3}\big(\mathrm{JSON}(E)\big),
\]
ensuring integrity and reproducibility.

\subsection{Evolution Loop}
The complete UKG-SE v3.0 evolution loop is expressed as:
\[
\mathrm{Loop} =
\left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
T \rightarrow R \rightarrow
\begin{cases}
T_{\mathrm{mut}} & R > R_{\mathrm{crit}},\\
T & R \le R_{\mathrm{crit}},
\end{cases}
\\[6pt]
(q,p) \rightarrow D \rightarrow
\begin{cases}
\mathrm{prune}(q,p) & D > D_{\mathrm{crit}},\\
(q,p) & D \le D_{\mathrm{crit}},
\end{cases}
\\[6pt]
\mathrm{Ledger}(T,R,q,p,\mathrm{flags})
\end{array}
\right.
\]

This loop defines the autonomous, self-refining behavior of the UKG-SE v3.0 system.